Pass 1 → Largest element (52) reaches the end.
Pass 2 → Second largest element (46) reaches its position.
Pass 3 → Third largest element (24) reaches its position.
Pass 4 → Fourth largest element (20) reaches its position.
Pass 5 → Array becomes completely sorted.


1.	Take an array of size n.
2.	Start an outer loop from the last index (n-1) down to 1.
3.	After every pass, the largest element moves to the end.
4.	Start an inner loop from index 0 up to i-1.
5.	Compare adjacent elements: array[j] and array[j+1].
6.	If array[j] > array[j+1], swap them.
7.	Continue until the inner loop finishes.
8.	By the end of each pass, the largest unsorted element reaches its correct position.
9.	Repeat until the entire array becomes sorted.
10.	Key Idea: Each pass pushes the largest unsorted element to the end.

Worst Case  : O(n²)
Average Case: O(n²)
Best Case   : O(n)

Space Complexity: O(1)